[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded Ebers-Moll BJT and junction-storage requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-STORAGE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit charge-only junction companion
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall provide a validated charge-only junction profile whose effective saturation-current scale participates only in transport Q and dQ/dV, with exactly zero static F and dF/dV. It shall share the qualified SPICE depletion/diffusion charge law and accepted BE charge history, expose true displacement current, and not be classified as a DC conduction path. It shall preserve diode/constant-capacitance behavior and retain explicit unavailable energy evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: JunctionStorage in native circuit/model/compile, shared newton/ac/API/audit loops, typed Client DTO. Verification: tests/junction_storage.rs DC-zero, complex AC and BE-KCL; existing diode and constant-C regressions; source-controlled Ebers-Moll composition and native oracle. Three meaningful RED tests failed on unknown old wire tag, then passed after implementation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BJT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Genuine bounded Ebers-Moll current and charge composition
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall lower qualified three-terminal NPN/PNP profiles to native conduction-only IS/BF and IS/BR junction paths with separate zero-voltage current senses, BF/BR transport CCCS contributions, and parallel BE/BC charge-only companions using effective IS and TF/TR. Charge shall not flow through or be amplified by the conduction senses. An outer zero-voltage collector sense shall expose signed total collector current. Private nodes shall not become source-name mappings.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Qualified first terms: IS,BF,BR,NF,NR,CJE,VJE,MJE,CJC,VJC,MJC,FC,TF,TR, TNOM27 and LEVEL1. Unsupported terms and instance parameters refuse atomically. The bounded explicit substrate terminal follows SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-001. Early/high-injection/leakage/base-resistance/temperature/excess-phase coupling remains open. These absent-coupling defaults reduce to Ebers-Moll; this is not general GP qualification. Implementation: BjtPreparation.cs plus additive Q bridge/readiness. Verification: BjtTests and BjtNativeOracleIntegration; separate provider outcomes retained.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit default BJT substrate terminal
STATEMENT: >>>
With an explicit fourth terminal on the bounded NPN or PNP profile, the frontend shall retain the default 1 pS substrate path to the intrinsic collector for NPN and base for PNP. Unsupported substrate storage and saturation terms shall refuse preparation. The three-terminal composition remains the separately qualified contract of SEMI-BJT-001.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BjtPreparation and OperatingPointBridge. Verification: BjtTests.Explicit_substrate_uses_default_native_leakage_reference. Native ngspice-47+ reference: BJTsetup defaults vertical NPN and lateral PNP with zero substrate capacitance and saturation current, and BJTload applies the circuit default Gmin across that junction.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Qualification investigation: the initial50ps BE grid missed the declared3mV early collector-voltage bound by4.968mV on an owned NPN circuit. At10ps the discrepancy reduced to0.983mV; at2ps early-slice refinement it reduced to0.184mV, consistent with first-order time discretization. The original failed run and fixed bounds remain in local artifacts. The initial Faer AC refusal was retained and referred to the numerical-provider owner. After importing06e8a6b (local47b9809), both LU and Faer passed the original NPN/PNP DC, complex AC and10ps BE comparisons, including signed collector currents and formal coarse/fine error reduction. The unchanged complex residual acceptance is independently qualified by the provider regression. This finite subset does not establish full Gummel-Poon or arbitrary timestep accuracy.
<<<
